{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:22216-1","published":"2026-11-03T10:21:52Z","modified":"2026-11-04T17:23:23.836832996Z","related":["CVE-2026-4430","CVE-2026-6039","CVE-2026-6040","CVE-2026-6045","CVE-2026-6047","CVE-2026-8356","CVE-2026-8357","CVE-2026-8358"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-4430","CVE-2026-6039","CVE-2026-6040","CVE-2026-6045","CVE-2026-6047","CVE-2026-8356","CVE-2026-8357","CVE-2026-8358"],"summary":"Security update for libreoffice","details":"This update for libreoffice fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in libreoffice:\n\n- Upgrade to 26.8.1.1.\n\n- Perfect spec file sync between Factory, SLE and Leap 16.X.\n\n- Update to LibreOffice 26.2.5.1 (was 25.2.5.2).\n\n- Fix the following security issues:\n  * CVE-2026-6039 (bsc#1268494): Denial of Service via a specially\n    crafted DXF polyline import.\n  * CVE-2026-6045 (bsc#1268497): Heap buffer overflow via crafted\n    EMF+ graphics import.\n  * CVE-2026-6047 (bsc#1268504): Denial of Service via heap buffer\n    overflow in OOXML document processing.\n  * CVE-2026-8356 (bsc#1268522): Denial of Service via a specially\n    crafted PPT file.\n  * CVE-2026-6040 (bsc#1268527): Heap use-after-free when importing\n    the blank-width characters of an ODF number format.\n  * CVE-2026-8357 (bsc#1268528): Heap buffer overflow in Calc\n    formula compilation.\n  * CVE-2026-8358 (bsc#1268529): Heap buffer overflow in spreadsheet\n    tracked-changes import.\n  * CVE-2026-4430 (bsc#1264357): Out-of-bounds write via crafted\n    OOXML documents with mismatched encryption salt parameters.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libreoffice","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/libreoffice&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"26.8.1.1-bp160.1.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libreoffice":"26.8.1.1-bp160.1.1","libreoffice-base":"26.8.1.1-bp160.1.1","libreoffice-base-drivers-postgresql":"26.8.1.1-bp160.1.1","libre